        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "pge:cc-d-care-2026-03-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 7 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) The CARE surcharge portion of the public purpose program charge is exempt under Sheet 1 and is neither exempted nor removed from the discount base, because no document on disk publishes it. Each base schedule prints one figure, \"Public Purpose Programs (all usage) $0.00614\"; Schedule E-CARE prints a per-kWh PPP discount ($0.01488) for nonresidential schedules only and refers the component to Preliminary Statement Part I, which this corpus does not hold. Each CARE-discountable subtotal therefore names the whole PPP Price, and no exemption Price cancels the surcharge. A CARE marginal rate is overstated by 0.65 times the surcharge, which lies between 0 and $0.00614/kWh, so by at most $0.0039910/kWh on every base. (2) Rate B, the 50.000 percent Delivery Minimum Bill Discount, has nothing to apply to: none of the five bases carries a delivery minimum bill. Each prices a base services charge instead, and Sheet 1 assigns a CARE customer to Income Tier 1 of it with no further discount. (3) Nothing selects Income Tier 1. Sheet 1: \"Customers whose otherwise applicable rate includes a base services charge will be assigned to Tier 1\". The base services charge is a urpx:ProfileAlternative on each base (on pge:e-1 it is in the sibling pge:e-1-income-tier modifier, which a composition with this modifier does not include), and nothing in URPX ties a modifier to an alternative, so a scenario cost model can pair this modifier with the Income Tier 2 or Tier 3 base services charge. (4) The master-meter provisions (Sheet 1, Rates C and D) are not modeled: a discount of 35.000 percent of total bundled charges multiplied by the number of CARE units divided by the total number of units, and 50.000 percent of the delivery minimum bill, for master-metered customers on Schedules EM, ES, ESR, ET and EM-TOU, none of which this corpus holds. (5) Direct access and community choice aggregation customers are not modeled. Sheet 1: \"The CARE discount will be calculated for direct access and community choice aggregation customers based on the total charges as if they were subject to bundled service rates. Discounts will be applied as a reduction to distribution charges.\" This version declares bundled service, and a departed customer's composition would need both this modifier and the base's vintage-PCIA modifier. (6) Eligibility is carried as residential customer kind and enrollment in pge:program-care. The qualifying criteria of Electric Rule 19.1, which this corpus does not hold, the Special Condition 2 limit to the primary residence, and its rule that a FERA participant cannot concurrently participate in CARE are not data. (7) pge:e-tou-c-2026-03-01, in force from this version's effective date until 2026-03-27, carries no CARE-discountable subtotal and is not a candidate of any exemption Price, so this modifier composes with the current E-TOU-C version only.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-05T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
